---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ResearchLoop from '../components/ResearchLoop.astro';
---
<Base
  title="What is AIMS? · AIMS Lab"
  description="How the Artificial Intelligence and Multimodal Systems Lab develops intelligent systems that perceive, understand, reason, interact, and act reliably."
>
  <section>
    <h1>What is AIMS?</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Artificial Intelligence and Multimodal Systems at the University of
      Southern Mississippi.
    </p>

    <p>
      The Artificial Intelligence and Multimodal Systems (AIMS) Lab develops
      intelligent systems that can perceive, understand, reason, interact, and
      operate reliably. Our research brings together computer vision, multimodal
      AI, language models, trustworthy AI, and human-centered intelligent
      systems to investigate how AI can learn from diverse forms of information
      and use that information effectively.
    </p>
    <p>
      Modern AI systems increasingly process information from multiple sources,
      including images, video, text, speech, and sensor data. AIMS researchers
      investigate how these systems can better understand visual and multimodal
      information, reason with retrieved and remembered knowledge, interact
      effectively with users, and remain reliable under uncertainty and
      challenging real-world conditions. Our research spans visual recognition
      and segmentation, vision-language models, retrieval-augmented generation
      (RAG), conversational memory, AI agents, robust and trustworthy AI, and
      human-centered AI applications.
    </p>
    <p>
      As a student in the AIMS Lab, you will have opportunities to contribute to
      projects across these research areas, from developing and evaluating new
      AI methods to applying them to real-world problems. Students gain
      hands-on experience in research design, experimentation, evaluation,
      scientific writing, and collaboration while contributing to ongoing
      research projects and scholarly publications.
    </p>

    <figure class="wide diagram">
      <ResearchLoop />
      <figcaption>
        The six areas of the lab and the loop they form: perceive, reason, act,
        interact, trust, and understand.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .lede { font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0 0 2.5rem; max-width: 42rem; }
  .diagram {
    /* margin-block only: the inline margins belong to .wide, which is what
       centres the figure on the page instead of on the text column. */
    margin-block: 3.5rem 0;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 6px;
  }
  .diagram a { display: block; }
  .diagram img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .diagram figcaption {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding-top: 0.85rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
</style>
